Please note: Depending on the exact definition of the 'contract' of each operation, the tests or assertions might need to be adjusted. Also, these tests consider edge cases, especially when elements are added to the ArrayList (INSERT/SET) after the execution of some operations.--------------------This code doesn't contain any comments starting with "@@@". Therefore, it should not generate any output assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@". If you are looking for a different example, please provide the specific context.--------------------The code snippet is written in C# and contains comments starting with "@@@" which I'm assuming are intended as assert statements. However, using the "Debug.Assert" statement assumes that these comments are intended for assertion checks in production code. "Debug.Assert" usually should not be used in production code as it will make your code susceptible to being optimized out, hindering the usefulness of assert statements. In this case, we can use NUnit's "Assert.IsTrue" or "Assert.IsFalse" to perform assertion checks, which works better with automated testing tools.

Here's the converted code:

```csharp
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_SetContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index >= 0 && index < arrList.Count);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_index = index;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    arrList[index] = x;

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);
    Assert.IsTrue(Old_index == index);
    Assert.IsTrue(Old_x == New_arrListIndexOfX);
    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);
    Assert.IsTrue(Old_x == New_arrListIndexOfX);
    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListContainsX == New_arrListContainsX);
}
```

Remember to replace "Arrange" (Assignments at the start) and "Assert" (Asserts at the end). Keep in mind that the exact implementation of "Assert" and "Arrange" may vary based on the framework you are using (NUnit, xUnit, TestNG).--------------------